    "body": "### Problem\n\nEditing with multiple cursors in replace mode only updates the display on the primary cursor.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- place multiple cursors\n- enter replace mode\n- type some text\n=> the displayed text will only be updated on the primary cursor location \n- exit replace mode to normal mode\n=> all cursor positions are updated\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nAll cursor positions should reflect edits in replace mode at all times. \n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n0.13.0-dev-1788+g09e4491a53\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\ndoes not apply\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nArch Linux\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nKitty 0.48.2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-kitty\n\n### Installation\n\nAUR",
